{"name":"Birthday Candle","hex":"#cfa2ad","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"birthday","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The anniversary of the day on which someone is born. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The anniversary of the day on which something is created."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To celebrate one's birthday."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/birthday"},{"term":"candle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light source consisting of a wick embedded in a solid, flammable substance such as wax, tallow, or paraffin.","The protruding, removable portion of a filter, particularly a water filter."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To observe the growth of an embryo inside (an egg), using a bright light source.","To dry (greenware) prior to the firing cycle, setting the kiln at 200° Celsius until all water is removed from the greenware."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Birthday cake","blocks":[{"text":"A birthday cake is a cake eaten as part of birthday celebrations. While there is no standard for birthday cakes, they are typically highly decorated layer cakes covered in frosting, often featuring birthday wishes followed by the celebrant's name. In many cultures, it is also customary to serve the birthday cake with small lit candles on top, especially in the case of a child's birthday. The cake often accompanies the singing of \"Happy Birthday to You\". Variations include cupcakes, cake pops, pastries, and tarts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Delicious_Birthday_Cake_%2814346969741%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_Birthday_Cake_%2814346969741%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birthday_cake","wikidata":"Q1195276"},{"title":"Birthday","blocks":[{"text":"A birthday is the anniversary of the birth of a person or the figurative birth of an institution. Birthdays of people are celebrated in numerous cultures, often with birthday gifts, birthday cards, a birthday party, or a rite of passage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Happy_family_2.jpg/330px-Happy_family_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birthday","wikidata":"Q47223"},{"title":"Candle","blocks":[{"text":"A candle is an ignitable wick embedded in wax, or another flammable solid substance such as tallow, that provides light, and in some cases, a fragrance. A candle can also provide heat or a method of keeping time. Candles have been used for over two millennia around the world, and were a significant form of indoor lighting until the invention of other types of light sources. Although electric light has largely made candle use nonessential for illumination, candles are still commonly used for functional, symbolic and aesthetic purposes and in specific cultural and religious settings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/LA2_Skultuna_kontorsljusstake.jpg/330px-LA2_Skultuna_kontorsljusstake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candle","wikidata":"Q12888135"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Pancraz_K%C3%B6rle_Die_Geburtstagstorte.jpg/500px-Pancraz_K%C3%B6rle_Die_Geburtstagstorte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Pancraz_K%C3%B6rle_Die_Geburtstagstorte.jpg/1280px-Pancraz_K%C3%B6rle_Die_Geburtstagstorte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Pancraz_K%C3%B6rle_Die_Geburtstagstorte.jpg/500px-Pancraz_K%C3%B6rle_Die_Geburtstagstorte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c